{
 "section_summary": "The section opens with a file note and an excerpt from a 1930 report on the rationalization of Japanese industry. A 1934 consular despatch encloses a Mitsubishi Economic Research Bureau circular reviewing Japan’s economy, cotton trade and shipping in 1933. A second despatch encloses the opening pages of a Nagoya Chamber of Commerce and Industry pamphlet defending Japanese labor conditions and examining the structure of industry in Japan, Aichi Prefecture and Nagoya.",
